The dictionary data in hsk_curriculum.json (each word's English meanings,
`meaning_en`, and the traditional form and pinyin of the dictionary entry they
come from) is adapted from CC-CEDICT, the community-maintained
Chinese-English dictionary published by MDBG
(https://www.mdbg.net/chinese/dictionary?page=cc-cedict), by way of
drkameleon/complete-hsk-vocabulary, which credits CC-CEDICT as the source of
its definitions.

CC-CEDICT is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0
International License: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

Changes made here: for each HSK 3.0 word one dictionary entry is chosen (the
one matching the official HSK 3.0 reading), its meanings are joined with "; ",
and some pinyin is repaired (README.md, "How an upstream entry becomes an
item" and "Pinyin repairs"). This adapted data is offered under the same
license.
